-我们没事 -我们没事
-We're okay. -We're okay.

1403
01:29:20,271 --> 01:29:22,398
我们没事
We're okay.

1404
01:29:22,440 --> 01:29:25,234
我们现在没事了 你也没事了
We're okay now. You're okay.

1405
01:29:29,614 --> 01:29:31,657
我们没事
We're okay.

1406
01:29:31,741 --> 01:29:33,034
好的
Okay.

1407
01:29:37,747 --> 01:29:39,624
谢谢
Thank you.

1408
01:29:42,585 --> 01:29:44,921
凯尔纳从莱昂纳德山外的一个加油站打来电话
Kellner called in from a gas station outside Mount Leonard.

1409
01:29:45,004 --> 01:29:46,255
我将与圣地亚哥和他的船员见面
I'll meet Santiago and his crew.

1410
01:29:46,339 --> 01:29:48,466
我们几个小时后就能到
We can be there in a couple hours.

1411
01:29:51,052 --> 01:29:53,221
雨果？
H-Hugo?

1412
01:29:53,346 --> 01:29:54,722
请大家暂时离开准备区
Could everyone leave the staging area

1413
01:29:54,847 --> 01:29:56,224
一分钟好吗？
for a minute, please?

1414
01:29:56,307 --> 01:29:59,143
-现在 请！出去！ -好的 我们走吧
-Now, please! Out! -Yeah. Okay, let's go.

1415
01:30:05,525 --> 01:30:07,193
你好 雨果
Hello, Hugo.

1416
01:30:12,782 --> 01:30:14,951
诺亚 拜托了
Noah, please.

1417
01:30:15,952 --> 01:30:17,829
你带着那东西潜水真是大错特错
It's terribly misguided for you to dive with that thing.

1418
01:30:17,995 --> 01:30:19,747
这不是魔法棒
It's not a magic wand.

1419
01:30:19,956 --> 01:30:21,749
它不是武器 但它的功能
And it's not a weapon, but it has functions

1420
01:30:21,833 --> 01:30:24,710
远远超出了你有限的使用范围
very far beyond your limited use of it.

1421
01:30:24,794 --> 01:30:29,298
凯尔纳是个体验家 不是吗？
Kellner was an experiencer, wasn't he?

1422
01:30:29,382 --> 01:30:31,384
这就是我为什么不能扑向他的原因
That's why I couldn't dive on him.

1423
01:30:31,467 --> 01:30:33,678
是
Yes.

1424
01:30:33,761 --> 01:30:35,680
他是
He was.

1425
01:30:37,432 --> 01:30:41,561
In Vivo 17 让你去招募他？
And In Vivo 17 told you to recruit him?

1426
01:30:42,728 --> 01:30:44,564
你绝对无法理解
Not in any way you'd understand.

1427
01:30:44,730 --> 01:30:46,274
如果这就是他们的计划 雨果
If this is all their plan, Hugo,

1428
01:30:46,357 --> 01:30:48,776
你可以肯定 这符合他们的利益 而不是我们的利益
you can be sure it's in their interests, not ours.

1429
01:30:48,943 --> 01:30:51,404
这是一种非常孤独的世界观
That's a very lonely way to look at the world.

1430
01:30:51,529 --> 01:30:52,905
不 别对我摆架子
No, don't condescend to me.

1431
01:30:53,030 --> 01:30:54,407
我在听你说话 诺亚
I'm listening to you, Noah.

1432
01:30:54,490 --> 01:30:56,534
我对此了解颇多
Something I've learned quite a bit about.

1433
01:30:56,659 --> 01:30:58,119
来自你的朋友？
From your friends?

1434
01:30:58,286 --> 01:30:59,829
是
Yes.

1435
01:30:59,871 --> 01:31:02,748
他们认为同理心是一种进化优势
They regard empathy as an evolutionary advantage,

1436
01:31:02,832 --> 01:31:05,418
是最重要的进化优势
as the foremost evolutionary advantage,

1437
01:31:05,501 --> 01:31:09,422
事实上 是生命存在的核心
in fact, the core of animate existence.

1438
01:31:09,630 --> 01:31:11,757
我们拒绝这种理解
Our rejection of this understanding

1439
01:31:11,883 --> 01:31:14,010
正在将我们引向灭绝
is leading us to our extinction.

1440
01:31:15,052 --> 01:31:18,139
你帮助它逃跑是因为你那颗多愁善感的心吗？
And is your bleeding heart why you helped it escape?

1441
01:31:20,057 --> 01:31:21,559
五年前
Five years ago.

1442
01:31:21,767 --> 01:31:23,728
那是你 对吧？
That was you, wasn't it?

1443
01:31:25,354 --> 01:31:26,731
是
Yes.

1444
01:31:27,773 --> 01:31:30,735
撇开这种行为的疯狂不谈
The utter insanity of that act aside,

1445
01:31:30,860 --> 01:31:33,112
你怎么能骗我五年
how could you lie to me for five years

1446
01:31:33,196 --> 01:31:34,822
每次你走进门的时候都骗我？
every time you walked through the door?

1447
01:31:34,906 --> 01:31:37,742
你对我说的一切 都是转移话题
Everything you said to me, it was all diversion.

1448
01:31:39,619 --> 01:31:42,788
你究竟是什么时候失去方向感的？
When precisely did you lose your bearings?

1449
01:31:42,955 --> 01:31:45,333
大约在你丢失你的那一个的时候
Around the time you lost yours.

1450
01:31:47,835 --> 01:31:49,420
当你失去她的时候
When you lost her.

1451
01:31:53,674 --> 01:31:56,260
你失去了她 几乎立刻 你也失去了我
You lost her and almost immediately were lost to me.

1452
01:31:56,469 --> 01:31:57,720
因为你关机了
Because you shut down.

1453
01:31:57,803 --> 01:31:59,138
不要妄自了解我
Do not presume to know me.

1454
01:31:59,305 --> 01:32:00,640
当她去世时 你把所有人
When she died, you reduced everyone

1455
01:32:00,806 --> 01:32:02,308
都限制为需要知道的人 包括我
to need-to-know, including me.

1456
01:32:02,433 --> 01:32:03,643
因为你说得很清楚
Because you were very clear.

1457
01:32:03,768 --> 01:32:05,019
你只需要知道他们
All you needed to know was them,

1458
01:32:05,186 --> 01:32:07,396
而他们是不可知的 至少我们无法知晓
and they are not knowable, not by us.

1459
01:32:07,605 --> 01:32:10,107
他们会的
They will be.

1460
01:32:10,274 --> 01:32:12,360
In Vivo 17 是非人类
In Vivo 17 is nonhuman

1461
01:32:12,485 --> 01:32:14,153
但比你我更接近上帝 诺亚
but nearer to God, Noah, than you or I.

1462
01:32:14,278 --> 01:32:16,322
你不必害怕他们
You don't need to fear them.

1463
01:32:17,240 --> 01:32:19,116
我害怕我们
I fear us.

1464
01:32:19,325 --> 01:32:22,245
WARDEX存在的全部原因在于我们掌握的知识
The entire reason WARDEX exists is because of our knowledge,

1465
01:32:22,453 --> 01:32:26,541
我们确信人类无法接受我们所知道的
certain that the human race cannot accept what we know.

1466
01:32:26,707 --> 01:32:28,417
这个真相将颠覆全世界所有
That truth will upend all established order

1467
01:32:28,501 --> 01:32:29,669
既定的秩序
across the entire world.

1468
01:32:29,835 --> 01:32:32,380
凯尔纳偷走的档案是一种病毒
The archive Kellner stole is a virus

1469
01:32:32,421 --> 01:32:36,634
全世界对它没有任何免疫力
against which the world has zero immunity.

1470
01:32:36,717 --> 01:32:39,178
我花了35年时间保护...
I have spent 35 years protecting...

1471
01:32:39,303 --> 01:32:40,555
你自己的财富和权力...
Your own wealth and power--

1472
01:32:40,680 --> 01:32:42,348
你一直保护的只是这些
that's all you've been protecting.

1473
01:32:42,473 --> 01:32:45,226
诺亚 诺亚
Noah. Noah.

1474
01:32:45,351 --> 01:32:47,520
我们每个人都有一种基本的信仰需求
There is an essential need in all of us to believe

1475
01:32:47,645 --> 01:32:50,940
以及同样强烈的被信仰需求
and an equal need to be believed.

1476
01:32:51,065 --> 01:32:53,150
你违反了所有证据标准
You've violated every standard of evidence.

1477
01:32:53,276 --> 01:32:54,860
你把所有只想了解
You've infantilized anyone

1478
01:32:54,944 --> 01:32:57,572
自己所目睹之事的人都当成了孩子
who only wanted to understand what they've witnessed.

1479
01:32:57,780 --> 01:33:00,575
你残酷地压制了他们的提问
You've brutally stifled their questions,

1480
01:33:00,616 --> 01:33:03,244
大声斥责他们 嘲笑和羞辱他们
shouted them down, ridiculed and shamed

1481
01:33:03,369 --> 01:33:05,079
并压制他们 只因为他们
and overridden them for the crime

1482
01:33:05,162 --> 01:33:07,123
犯了“惊讶”的罪行
of simply being astonished.

1483
01:33:07,290 --> 01:33:10,042
我们相信信徒 然后剥夺世人
We believe the believers and then deny the world

1484
01:33:10,167 --> 01:33:11,961
相信他们的机会
the chance to believe them, too.

1485
01:33:12,003 --> 01:33:14,589
但人们不断好奇 不断遭遇未知
But people keep wondering, encountering the unknown,

1486
01:33:14,755 --> 01:33:16,382
将自己的经历告诉其他人
telling others of their experiences.

1487
01:33:16,507 --> 01:33:18,759
他们渴望真相
They are starved for the truth.

1488
01:33:18,843 --> 01:33:22,388
这场持续79年的恐怖运动
This 79-year terror campaign

1489
01:33:22,471 --> 01:33:25,933
充斥着混淆视听 谎言和掩盖真相 必须结束！
of obfuscation, lies and cover-up has to end!

1490
01:33:26,142 --> 01:33:27,977
我们准备向您进行演示
We're ready to show you a demonstration.

1491
01:33:28,102 --> 01:33:30,438
-出去！出去！ -对不起 先生 我们有...
-Get out! Get out! -Sorry, sir, we have...

1492
01:33:30,521 --> 01:33:32,690
转身离开！
Turn around and get out now!

1493
01:33:38,029 --> 01:33:40,948
找出昨天没来上班的12个人
Pull up the 12 who didn't show up to work yesterday.

1494
01:33:40,990 --> 01:33:43,951
我需要现在和他在一起的人的面孔
I need faces who are with him right now.

1495
01:33:44,076 --> 01:33:46,537
-她 -Grace Zhao 神经服务
-Her. -Grace Zhao, neuro-services.

1496
01:33:46,662 --> 01:33:48,247
-他 -内森·特温宁
-Him. -Nathan Twinning,

1497
01:33:48,331 --> 01:33:49,832
雨果的首席助手
Hugo's chief aide.

1498
01:33:49,957 --> 01:33:51,417
找到了进入他们移动运营商的后门
Got a back door into their mobile providers.

1499
01:33:51,500 --> 01:33:53,294
稍等
Hang on.

1500
01:33:56,213 --> 01:34:00,801
他们昨晚在这里关机了...
They shut down their phones last night... right here.

1501
01:34:02,011 --> 01:34:03,721
我会提前预测他们的路线 使之重叠
I'll project their routes ahead to overlap.

1502
01:34:03,929 --> 01:34:06,641
我可以提供方圆四分之一英里内的AI模型
I can give you the AI model within a quarter-mile radius.

1503
01:34:15,358 --> 01:34:17,902
莫拉修女 修女
Sister Maura. Sister.

1504
01:34:26,035 --> 01:34:27,495
简？
Jane?

1505
01:34:27,578 --> 01:34:29,080
简 你在哪里？
Where are you, Jane?

1506
01:34:31,916 --> 01:34:33,376
上帝爱我们吗？
Does God love us?

1507
01:34:33,542 --> 01:34:36,587
我不是问他是否爱我们？我知道他爱我们
I don't mean, does he love us? I know he does.

1508
01:34:36,712 --> 01:34:40,341
他只爱我们吗？
Does he love only us?

1509
01:34:40,424 --> 01:34:42,677
因为创世记说我们是他最伟大的创造
'Cause Genesis says that we're his supreme creation,

1510
01:34:42,843 --> 01:34:45,554
但是你认为有可能...
but do you think it's possible that...

1511
01:34:45,638 --> 01:34:47,181
在地球上
On Earth.

1512
01:34:48,391 --> 01:34:49,517
什么？
What?

1513
01:34:49,725 --> 01:34:51,227
创世纪
Genesis.

1514
01:34:51,352 --> 01:34:56,023
它说我们是上帝在地球上最伟大的创造
It says we are God's supreme creation on Earth.

1515
01:35:04,990 --> 01:35:07,201
你认为可能还有其他人吗？
Do you think there could be others?

1516
01:35:08,786 --> 01:35:10,871
是
Yes.

1517
01:35:10,955 --> 01:35:12,540
我也这么认为
I would think so.

1518
01:35:12,707 --> 01:35:16,293
他为何创造了如此浩瀚的宇宙
Why would he make such a vast universe,

1519
01:35:16,419 --> 01:35:20,464
却只为我们保留？
yet save it only for us?

1520
01:35:21,549 --> 01:35:26,554
如果你发现我们并非孤身一人 如果...
If you found out we weren't alone, if...

1521
01:35:26,679 --> 01:35:30,349
如果有人向你展示 向你证明...
if someone showed you, proved it to you...

1522
01:35:32,143 --> 01:35:34,395
那会吓到你吗？
...would that frighten you?

1523
01:35:34,520 --> 01:35:37,273
不 为什么？应该这样吗？
No. Why? Should it?

1524
01:35:37,356 --> 01:35:40,609
但如果这一切都崩溃了呢？
But what if it all collapsed?

1525
01:35:40,651 --> 01:35:43,028
为了你 也为了世界上每一位有信仰的人
For you and every other person of faith in the world.

1526
01:35:43,112 --> 01:35:44,238
然后呢？
Then what?

1527
01:35:44,280 --> 01:35:45,448
哦
Oh.

1528
01:35:45,656 --> 01:35:47,867
我亲爱的简
My dear, Jane.

1529
01:35:47,992 --> 01:35:52,913
我不认为你曾怀疑过你对上帝的信仰
I don't think that you ever doubted your belief in God.

1530
01:35:52,955 --> 01:35:56,041
我觉得你对人失去了信心
I think you lost your faith in people.

1531
01:36:00,463 --> 01:36:04,049
他们说你借了他们的手机 所以要你付钱？
They say you're paying because you borrowed their phone?

1532
01:36:11,223 --> 01:36:12,850
你在电脑附近吗？
Are you near the computer?

1533
01:36:12,975 --> 01:36:14,477
是
Yes.

1534
01:36:14,643 --> 01:36:16,854
KCXE是什么？
What is KCXE?

1535
01:36:16,979 --> 01:36:19,607
只有这些字母...KCXE
Just those letters-- KCXE.

1536
01:36:26,906 --> 01:36:28,783
还记得小时候吗？
Remember being a kid?

1537
01:36:28,991 --> 01:36:30,409
当然
Sure.

1538
01:36:30,534 --> 01:36:32,953
大部分是我十岁以后的东西
Mostly stuff after I was ten.

1539
01:36:38,042 --> 01:36:42,129
你能告诉我一些我小时候的事情吗？
Can you tell anything about me from when I was small?

1540
01:37:01,065 --> 01:37:03,150
它只是一只狐狸
It's just a fox.

1541
01:37:16,580 --> 01:37:18,123
不 不 不 不！
No, no, no. No!

1542
01:37:18,249 --> 01:37:21,001
-停！停！ -不 丹尼尔！
-Stop! Stop! -No. Daniel!

1543
01:37:23,003 --> 01:37:24,380
-走吧 跟我们走 -等等
-Let's go. Come with us. -Hold on.

1544
01:37:24,463 --> 01:37:26,590
-等等 -走吧
-Hold on. -Let's go.

1545
01:37:26,674 --> 01:37:28,342
我认识他 我认识他
I know him. I know him.

1546
01:37:28,467 --> 01:37:29,844
我们只是想快速检查一下你
We just got to check you real quick,

1547
01:37:30,010 --> 01:37:32,429
确保里面没有人和你在一起
make sure nobody's in there with you.

1548
01:37:39,895 --> 01:37:41,397
清除
Clear.

1549
01:37:41,480 --> 01:37:43,482
好的 开始装载
All right, let's load up.

1550
01:37:43,649 --> 01:37:45,276
你看 消防车就是这样...
See, the thing about fire trucks--

1551
01:37:45,359 --> 01:37:47,695
所有人都会赶紧给你让路
everyone gets the hell out of your way.

1552
01:38:36,493 --> 01:38:38,245
我就知道你会成功的
I knew you'd make it.

1553
01:38:38,287 --> 01:38:39,788
我很高兴你知道
I'm glad you knew.

1554
01:38:39,997 --> 01:38:41,665
毋庸置疑
Never a doubt.

1555
01:38:48,797 --> 01:38:50,507
玛格丽特
Margaret.

1556
01:38:52,092 --> 01:38:53,677
玛格丽特
Margaret.

1557
01:38:56,513 --> 01:38:58,015
你好 玛格丽特
Hello, Margaret.

1558
01:39:00,142 --> 01:39:02,353
你知道我是谁吗？
Do you know who I am?

1559
01:39:02,394 --> 01:39:03,938
当然 你是雨果
Of course. You're Hugo.

1560
01:39:06,774 --> 01:39:08,359
内森
Nathan.

1561
01:39:09,693 --> 01:39:13,155
克洛伊·马利克
Chloe. Malik.

1562
01:39:13,364 --> 01:39:15,950
乔丹·莱蒂莎
Jordan. Letisha.

1563
01:39:17,076 --> 01:39:18,827
格蕾丝
Grace.

1564
01:39:18,994 --> 01:39:20,663
嗨 特里
Hi, Terri.

1565
01:39:20,746 --> 01:39:22,748
凯特琳 那是埃弗雷特
Kaitlyn. That's Everett.

1566
01:39:50,275 --> 01:39:52,444
我觉得我们基本做对了
I think we got it mostly right.

1567
01:39:53,821 --> 01:39:55,239
玛格丽特
Margaret.

1568
01:39:55,447 --> 01:39:57,992
你为什么不看我？
Why won't you look at me?

1569
01:39:58,117 --> 01:39:59,535
因为你就是...你就是那个人
Because you're-you're the guy.

1570
01:39:59,660 --> 01:40:01,912
你是无所不知的人
You're the guy who knows everything.

1571
01:40:03,497 --> 01:40:06,333
而我...我还没准备好知道所有的事情
And I'm... and I'm not ready to know everything.

1572
01:40:08,002 --> 01:40:11,547
包括 比如 为什么我爸妈的整个房子
Including, like, why-why my mom and dad's entire goddamn house

1573
01:40:11,588 --> 01:40:13,007
就这么摆在那里！
is just sitting right there!

1574
01:40:13,048 --> 01:40:16,301
发生了什么事？你为什么要这样做？
What is going on? Why are you doing this?

1575
01:40:16,427 --> 01:40:18,387
那是我长大的地方 那是我长大的地方
That's where I grew up. That's where I grew up.

1576
01:40:18,512 --> 01:40:21,682
这就是我的人生 这就是我的人生
This is my life. This is my life.

1577
01:40:21,724 --> 01:40:23,976
这很重要...我想要什么 我是谁
And this matters-- what I want, who I am,

1578
01:40:24,018 --> 01:40:27,771
不是作为你 他或她的身份 而是作为我自己的身份
not who I am as you or him or her, but as me.

1579
01:40:31,775 --> 01:40:33,777
不不不不不不不不
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

1580
01:40:33,861 --> 01:40:36,196
否 否
No. No.

1581
01:40:37,656 --> 01:40:40,451
我不会成为任何人的宗教
I will not be anyone's religion.

1582
01:41:51,063 --> 01:41:52,564
我的房间
My room.

1583
01:41:56,360 --> 01:41:58,278
